<title>USA: French Fragrances Q4 Jan 31 net rises.</title>
<headline>French Fragrances Q4 Jan 31 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollars in Thousands, except share data)</p>
<p>			Three Months Ended	    Year Ended</p>
<p>			 January 31,			 January  31,</p>
<p>			1997	    1996	  1997	  1996</p>
<p>			  (unaudited)</p>
<p> Net Sales     $36,544	  $19,586    $140,482     $87,979</p>
<p> Gross Profit   10,940	    4,977	46,078	21,639</p>
<p>Gross Profit</p>
<p>   Percentage(a)   30%		25%	   33%	   25%</p>
<p> EBITDA	    4,591	    1,879	21,885	 9,738</p>
<p>EBITDA Percentage(a)</p>
<p>			 13%		10%	   16%	   11%</p>
<p>Income From</p>
<p>   Operations    3,511	    1,498	18,222	 8,419</p>
<p> Net Earnings    1,240		502	 8,248	 3,007</p>
<p>Primary Earnings</p>
<p>   per Share(b)    .08	   .05(c)	   .61	.35(c)</p>
<p>Fully Diluted Earnings</p>
<p>   per Share	 .08	   .05(c)	   .60	.33(c)</p>
<p>Primary Share</p>
<p>Equivalents(b)</p>
<p>		15,619,653	9,788,629  13,639,952   8,517,760</p>
<p>Fully Diluted Share</p>
<p>Equivalents</p>
<p>		15,746,721     10,391,959  13,787,660   9,121,091</p>
<p>(a)  Based on the percentage of Net Sales for the periods.</p>
<p>(b)  Primary Earnings per Share and Primary Share Equivalents give effect to the assumed exercise or conversion of dilutive stock options and convertible securities under the treasury stock method. Based on the actual number of common shares outstanding, net earnings per share for the three months and year ended January 31, 1997, were $.09 and $.71, compared to $.06 and $.40, respectively, for the comparable periods last year.</p>
<p>(c)  Shares for the three months and year ended January 31, 1996 are presented on a pro forma basis using the conversion factor of 7.12 for each historical share outstanding for the period from November 1, 1996 to November 30, 1996.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
